# Placeholder for google-services.json

This file should be downloaded from your Firebase Console after setting up your Android app.

## How to get this file:

1. Go to [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com/)
2. Select your project
3. Click on the Android icon or go to Project Settings
4. Under "Your apps", find your Android app
5. Click "Download google-services.json"
6. Replace this file with the downloaded `google-services.json`

## Important:
- This file contains your Firebase configuration for Android
- Do NOT commit the actual `google-services.json` to version control if it contains sensitive data
- Add `google-services.json` to your `.gitignore` if needed

For detailed instructions, see: `firebase_setup_guide.md`
